              "ideas": {
                "1": {
                  "title": "Test GR. Does GW go at c and have 2 polarisations? If not, alternative theories of gravity might be needed e.g Brans-Dicke",
                  "id": 35
                },
                "2": {
                  "title": "Test string theory. Some theories sau that we experience a 4d brane that is situated within a higher dimsional bulk universe with extra space dimensions. Gravity would still propagate in the bulk; this would be why gravity is weak",
                  "id": 37
                },
                "3": {
                  "title": "Model populations at large redshift. From this we can learn about cosmological formation of sources, history of stars and its dependence of matter content of the universe",
                  "id": 40
                },
                "4": {
                  "title": "Dark matter and dark energy. CBC can be used as standard candle. With MM astronomy, the red shift can be measured, From this, the Hubble constant, dark matter and dark energy density can be parameterised.",
                  "id": 43
                },
                "5": {
                  "title": "Lower frequency cut-off -> can detect much heavier black holes. LIGO ~ 200 solar mass, ET 10^2 - 10^4 solar mass.",
                  "id": 45
                },
                "6": {
                  "title": "Supernova: test all physics at once...",
                  "id": 50
                },
                "-1": {
                  "title": "Test the no hair theorem. Can black holes be classified by mass, spin and charge? Same as testing Kerr solution.",
                  "id": 36
                },
                "-2": {
                  "title": "How did the supermassive black hole at the centre of the galaxy form? Population of stellar mass and IMBH as a function of redshift can give BH demographics, distribution and growth",
                  "id": 38
                },
                "-3": {
                  "title": "GW background allows us to see closer to the big bang than the CMB. CMB goes to 375000 years, GW background not affected by matter so can go much further",
                  "id": 41
                },
                "-4": {
                  "title": "May detect cosmic strings. This occur during phase transitions (as a result of cosmological inflation) of the unverive and are predicted by QFT + string theory. ",
                  "id": 44
                },
                "-5": {
                  "title": "Neutron stars",
                  "id": 46,
